{"t": 1794110442.638458, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_or_update_file", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return page `number` (1-based) of `items`, `size` items per page.\"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "message": "Fix page() to treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)", "owner": "acme", "path": "catalog/pager.py", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794110445.577958, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Problem\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` treated `number` as 0-based (`start = number * size`), but the API documents page numbers as 1-based, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page (issue #57).\n\n## Fix\n\nCompute the offset as `(number - 1) * size`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```python\n>>> page(list(range(1, 11)), 1, 3)\n[1, 2, 3]\n>>> page(list(range(1, 11)), 2, 3)\n[4, 5, 6]\n>>> page(list(range(1, 11)), 4, 3)\n[10]\n```\n\nFixes #57.", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
